  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The draft omits that the DMFS benefit weakened from 65% at two years to 59% at five years in KEYNOTE-942, while reporting the RFS figure as durable.
     quote         : “Those are numbers with five years behind them.”
     why           : The draft presents the 49% RFS and 59% DMFS figures as the five-year read without noting that the DMFS figure represents a weakening from the 65% reduction reported at the two-year primary analysis. Reporting the five-year figures as simply 'numbers with five years behind them' without noting the trajectory is selective: the RFS figure strengthened (44% to 49%) while DMFS weakened (65% to 59%). A reader cannot assess durability from the five-year figures alone without knowing the direction of travel.
     fix           : Add a clause noting that the DMFS reduction eased from 65% at two years to 59% at five years, alongside the RFS improvement from 44% to 49%, so the reader can see both directions.

